// Export Date: 2026-08-02
// The current Iceberg version at the time of writing (3cd0b960df368f7aba38874c4ac6f67ad9816bd7)
// has strange behavior:
// When given a 30-second-per-ply time limit, it can find a forced mate after `14a. Tiger &4`,
// and its principal variation contains `15b. Beta 3`.
// However, after playing that exact ply (i.e., `15b. Beta 3`), Iceberg mysteriously "loses" the mate
// it previously discovered (i.e., it can't find it within the time limit, in that position).
// This is extremely counterintuitive, since we should be _closer_ to the forced win that it previously found,
// making it _easier_ to find that forced win.

0b. =Rooster; Dragon Elephant Beta; Ox Rabbit Snake Horse Ram Monkey Dog Boar Fish Fish Squid Frog; Dog
0a. =Snake; Rat Rabbit Alpha; Rat Ox Tiger Tiger Dragon Horse Ram Monkey Rooster Elephant Squid Frog; Boar
1b. Beta 5
2a. Alpha 2
3b. Beta 4
4a. Alpha 3
5b. Rabbit *6, Squid *6
6a. Alpha *2
7b. Boar *6, Snake *6x
8a. Alpha *1
9b. Dragon &6
10a. Ox 3, Rabbit 2x
11b. Elephant &6
12a. Squid &4
13b. Rabbit &3
14a. Tiger &4
15b. Beta 3
16a. Squid 5x, Rat 2
17b. Dog 3, Snake 5
18a. Tiger &2
19b. Beta *4
20a. Rat &4
21b. Rabbit 2, Dog 2
22a. Ox 4, Squid *4x+#0
